<decompilertest>
<binaryimage arch="x86:LE:64:default:gcc">
<!--
    RE-friction need conditional-indirect-branches-hide: a dispatch whose two
    destinations are constants selected by a conditional move hides the whole
    body behind the branch.

    csjmp picks between two code addresses with CMOVZ and jumps through the
    register:
        401000  TEST  RDI,RDI
        401003  MOV   R8,0x401030
        40100d  MOV   R9,0x401020
        401017  CMOVZ R9,R8
        40101b  JMP   R9
        401020  MOV RAX,RSI ; ADD RAX,1 ; RET
        401030  MOV RAX,RSI ; SUB RAX,1 ; RET

    SLEIGH lifts the CMOVZ to a real conditional branch, so at the BRANCHIND the
    destination is a MULTIEQUAL of the two constants.  Both jump-table models
    (JumpBasic and its default-path extension) are value-range models and
    JumpBasic::isprune stops at any marker op, so the MULTIEQUAL output becomes
    the normalized switch variable with nothing to bound it.  Recovery is
    declined, FlowInfo::truncateIndirectJump rewrites the BRANCHIND to a CALLIND
    with a "Treating indirect jump as call" warning, and neither arm is ever
    decoded.

    Stage model: S2 "switch-model" sub-stage; the destination set is recovered as
    data and never promoted into the CFG.  Fix surface = a default-off ArchOption
    (constselectjump) that, when both value-range models fail, walks the
    MULTIEQUAL/COPY web behind the BRANCHIND and installs a fixed jump-table
    model over the constant destination set.

    Pass 1 (default, option off): assertion #1 proves the bug reproduces; the
    dispatch renders as a computed call through a code pointer and both arms are
    missing.
    Pass 2 (option constselectjump on): assertions #2 and #3 prove the table is
    recovered as a switch and both arms are decoded.
-->
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x401000">
4885ff49b8301040000000000049b920104000000000004d0f44c841ffe190904889f04883c001c30f1f8400000000004889f04883e801c3
</bytechunk>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x401000" name="csjmp"/>
</binaryimage>
<script>
  <com>lo fu csjmp</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>option constselectjump on</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>quit</com>
</script>
<stringmatch name="CONSTSELECTJUMP #1: the selected destination renders as a computed call (bug reproduced)" min="1" max="1">\(\*v1\)\(\)</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="CONSTSELECTJUMP #2: constselectjump on recovers the constant destination set as a switch" min="1" max="1">case 0x401030:</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="CONSTSELECTJUMP #3: both arms behind the branch are decoded" min="1" max="1">return a1 \+ 1;</stringmatch>
</decompilertest>
